    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The casting of Lupita Nyong'o in Christopher Nolan's upcoming Homer adaptation triggered a fierce digital backlash, an eruption of social disorder where agents of social disorder used the unregulated platform for attacks to propagate false claims about erasing European history. This reputational flashpoint requiring containment now threatens the institutional authority for the project, exposing how a single decision can ignite an ideological conflict that destabilizes creative control and public consensus over classical narratives.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
